Project Mu: the quiet toolbar

Mu keeps Chromium's toolbar but takes the noise out of it:

  * Forward is hidden while it could do nothing (most of the time) and
    appears after going back. The "Show forward button" setting still hides
    it for good.
  * No divider between the extensions button and the menu.
  * The app menu button is an ensō (new mu_menu.icon) instead of three dots.
    Only this button changes: the three-dot icon is shared by many other
    menus.
  * The address rests in the middle of the address bar, and moves to the
    left edge while it is being edited.

